      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focus closely on monitoring her vitals, mouth actions, and性情 (behavior) daily to detect early signs of complications like fever or a persistent rumen fistula. Restrict her feed for at least 24 hours post-surgery, gradually reintroducing small amounts of high-quality hay over the next week once she is clearly eating the bagpipe (clear) voluntarily without signs of pain or bloating. Start exposing her to full grazing only after she has fully regained her appetite, chews properly, and maintains body temperature, which usually happens by day 7. Always consult with your livestock veterinarian for specific dosage of any prescribed antibiotics.",
